message: If you use this work, please cite the relevant paper.
preferred-citation:
  abstract: >-
    <jats:p>Digital dynamic consent is a key element to improve the involvement
    of participants as proactive partners in research and requires the adoption
    of standard-based information models to support data reuse. In this work we
    present the HL7 FHIR Consent Profile we developed to integrate individual
    consent preferences on biobanked samples and relative information within the
    infrastructure of the the Biobanking and BioMolecular Resources European
    Research Infrastructure Consortium (BBMRI-ERIC). The Profile builds on the
    official HL7 FHIR Consent Resource and adopts the Common Condition of use
    Elements (CCE) terminology to express the participants’ wills. A preliminary
    evaluation on a minimally optimized setup suggests that using the Profile’s
    attributes in queries adds no significant performance overhead. The current
    version of the Profile is available online, together with a suite of
    demonstrative tools, and will be implemented for validation in the final
    prototype of a wider pilot of the Italian Node of BBMRI-ERIC within the
    Strengthening BBMRI.it Project.</jats:p>
